      "content": "# Zenith Smart Hub Quick-Start Troubleshooting Guide\n\n---\n\n## Troubleshooting 'Error 404: Connectivity Lost'\n\n'Error 404: Connectivity Lost' often indicates a temporary hiccup in the Smart Hub's ability to connect to the network. Follow the steps outlined in this thorough guide to quickly resolve the issue.\n\n### Step-by-Step Instructions\n\n#### Step 1: Disconnect and Reconnect\n1. **Unplug the Smart Hub from the power source.**\n2. **Wait for 10 seconds** - Allow the power capacitors to discharge completely.\n3. **Plug the Smart Hub back in** and wait for the device to power on fully.\n\n#### Step 2: Hard Reset\n1. Press and hold the reset button (found at the back of the Smart Hub) for 10 seconds.\n2. Release the reset button and wait for the Hub to reboot.\n\n#### Step 3: Check Network Settings\n1. Verify the Smart Hub’s network settings are correct.\n2. Ensure your internet connection is stable and active.\n\n#### Step 4: Reboot Device Router\n1. **Unplug the router** from its power source for 30 seconds.\n2. **Plug the router back in** and wait for it to",
